<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  Manifest of the statically linked mugen-static.exe (the GNU Make / MinGW
  build).

  Deliberately differs from src/mugen.manifest in one way: no dependency on the
  private assembly Elecbyte.MUGEN.libs.

  That dependency is inherited from the original binary, whose DLLs (SDL.dll,
  SDL_mixer.dll, zlib1.dll, libresample.dll, ...) are resolved through the
  private assembly folder Elecbyte.MUGEN.libs next to mugen.exe. The Windows
  loader checks such a dependency BEFORE running any code, so if the folder is
  absent it refuses to start the process at all:

      The application has failed to start because its side-by-side
      configuration is incorrect.

  This build links every one of those libraries statically, so its import table
  holds Windows system DLLs and msvcrt.dll and nothing else. The dependency
  describes something the executable does not use. Keeping it made the static
  build refuse to start without the very folder it exists to make unnecessary,
  and produced no log line, no error and no code execution to diagnose it from.

  The MSVC build keeps the original manifest, because it does link those DLLs.

  requestedExecutionLevel is kept: it is what makes Windows treat the process as
  a normal application rather than applying installer heuristics.
-->
<assembly xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1" manifestVersion="1.0">
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges>
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="asInvoker" uiAccess="false"></requestedExecutionLevel>
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
</assembly>
